' CROW'S NEST
' An original game by Claude (an AI made by Anthropic) for Amy Studio and
' Amy Bienvenu, 2026, after her idea of a bigger, camera-led version: the
' camera opens on the crows, pans back to the slingshot, and follows the
' pumpkin across; a spinning star waits midway; the pumpkins are carved
' and lit from inside; now and then a crow hits the screen.
'
' Halloween night. The crows have nested in a stack of crates beyond the
' field, and you have a slingshot and a pile of jack-o'-lanterns. Push the
' stick up and down to aim, hold the button to pull the elastic back (the
' power swings up and down), let go to throw. Glass shatters and lets the
' pumpkin through; wood cracks, is shoved along, or (a hard throw) is
' broken right through; stone takes a hard throw. A block with nothing
' under it falls, unless it is held between two blocks or by a neighbour
' standing on something; a crow that falls, or that a block lands on,
' flies off. Hit the spinning star on the way for a bonus.
'
' How it is drawn: the world is 80 columns wide; the screen shows 32 of
' them from CamX, redrawn from the world and the 10 x 8 grid of big cells
' (render.asm) whenever the camera moves a column. The crows are animated
' by rewriting their tiles' patterns; the pumpkin is three sprites (body,
' its glowing face showing through the carving, and the stem in a
' sprite of its own just above, so it never shares their scanlines); the star's
' four frames were drawn by turning a real five-pointed star (art.py).
'
' House rules kept: joystick only; text in columns 2-29 and rows 1-22;
' tiles at 128 and up; a title tune that plays once (Amy's play song ...
' once); a credits page; the frame loop is protected from the NMI and
' every screen is drawn with the NMI off after a wait.

